      "description": "Clarion Conqueror is a 3/3 flyer that shuts down activated abilities of artifacts, creatures, and planeswalkers. While decent, the opponent's board has Hired Claws whose pump abilities ({1}{R}: Put a +1/+1 counter) are relevant to shut down. However, the Cavern of Souls was set to 'Ally' type, not Dragon, so casting Clarion Conqueror (a Dragon) through Cavern doesn't make it uncounterable - the mana produced can only be spent on Ally creatures. More importantly, with 5 lands available (Cavern + 2 Sunbillow Verge + 2 Maelstrom, one tapped), MiniMx Heckler could have cast Nova Hellkite for {3}{R}{R} using warp cost {2}{R} to get immediate haste value, dealing 1 damage to a creature on entry and attacking for 4 flying damage. With 4 untapped lands producing mana, they likely had enough for Nova Hellkite's warp cost of {2}{R} (3 mana). Nova Hellkite with haste would have applied significantly more pressure, especially since this is the postcombat main phase where haste doesn't matter anyway. Actually, since this is postcombat main, haste on Nova Hellkite is wasted. Clarion Conqueror's ability to shut down Hired Claw's pump activation is relevant. The choice is reasonable but Clarion Conqueror costs {2}{W} = 3 mana while leaving mana open, whereas the bigger dragons need more mana. Given postcombat timing, Clarion Conqueror is actually a fine choice since it deploys a flyer and shuts down the Hired Claw pump abilities.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Clarion Conqueror (3/3 flying, shuts down activated abilities) for {2}{W}",
      "better_line": "This is close to reasonable given postcombat timing. However, casting Sarkhan, Dragon Ascendant for {1}{R} would have been cheaper (2 mana), could behold a Dragon from hand to create a Treasure token (ramping toward the powerful 4-5 mana dragons next turn), and would grow when dragons enter later. Sarkhan + holding up mana might have been slightly better for the long game plan.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 78,
      "player": "MiniMx Heckler",
      "decision_index": 85,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Plotting Slickshot Show-Off instead of casting it costs the opportunity to attack with it this turn (it has haste) alongside the existing creatures. With Hired Claw x2 and Emberheart Challenger already on board, adding a hasty flyer to the attack could push significant damage. The opponent is at 14 life and Qwen3 Drama has burn spells in hand (Lightning Helix, Burst Lightning) that could also trigger Slickshot's +2/+0 ability during combat. Plotting does allow a free cast next turn, but the aggro deck wants to maximize pressure now, especially with burn to close out the game.",
      "action_taken": "Plotted Slickshot Show-Off for {1}{R} instead of casting it.",
      "better_line": "Cast Slickshot Show-Off for {1}{R}, then attack with all creatures. During combat, cast Burst Lightning or Lightning Helix targeting opponent to trigger Slickshot's +2/+0 (making it 3/2 flying) and Emberheart Challenger's prowess, dealing significantly more damage this turn. The free cast next turn from plotting doesn't compensate for the lost haste attack and spell triggers this turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 80,
      "player": "Qwen3 Drama",
      "decision_index": 88,
    },
    {
