    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 8 life. Qwen3 Drama has Lightning Helix (3 damage) and Burst Lightning (2 damage) in hand, totaling 5 damage from burn spells alone. With an untapped Mountain available (one Mountain is untapped), they could cast Burst Lightning for 2 damage (1 mana) bringing opponent to 6, then they'd need another mana for Lightning Helix. Looking at the board: Sacred Foundry (tapped), Sunbillow Verge (unclear tap state), Mountain (tapped), Mountain (untapped). They have 1 untapped land visible, which isn't enough for both spells (need 3 total: 1 for Burst Lightning + 2 for Lightning Helix). However, they also have Sacred Foundry and Sunbillow Verge in hand they could play. If they play Sacred Foundry (paying 2 life, entering untapped) or Sunbillow Verge, they'd have additional mana. With a land drop + untapped Mountain, that's 2 mana - still not enough for both. But wait - they could cast Burst Lightning now for R (using the untapped Mountain), dealing 2 to bring opponent to 6, then on the next turn cast Lightning Helix. But the real issue is they're in combat and declined to use ANY burn. At minimum, casting Burst Lightning to the face for 2 damage (opponent goes to 6) is pure value here with lethal potentially coming next turn. Declining to use burn when the opponent is at 8 life and you have creatures attacking is a significant missed opportunity. Actually, re-examining: they have 1 untapped Mountain. They could cast Burst Lightning (R) to deal 2 to opponent (8→6). This is free damage with no downside. Passing on this is a clear mistake.",
