    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 8 life. Qwen3 Drama has Lightning Helix (3 damage) and Burst Lightning (2 damage) in hand, totaling 5 damage from burn spells alone. With two Hired Claws and Emberheart Challenger on board ready to attack, the Hired Claw triggers deal at least 1 damage each when attacking with Lizards (2 damage from triggers), plus combat damage from attackers. Even without combat, after combat the burn spells could finish the opponent. But more critically, declining to cast burn spells pre-combat when the opponent is at 8 life and you have 8 lands available is suspicious. However, the optimal line depends on combat - casting Burst Lightning and Lightning Helix post-combat would be fine too. The real issue is that 'Chosen: False' means they declined to cast ANY spell here. If they proceed to combat and then cast burn post-combat, that's fine. But if this is their only chance to cast instants this turn, they're missing lethal. With 2 Hired Claws attacking (2 damage from triggers + at least 2 combat damage = 4) plus Lightning Helix (3) + Burst Lightning (2) = 9 damage total, which is lethal against 8 life. They should cast burn spells to secure the kill. Declining here before combat is acceptable if they plan to cast post-combat, but the decision point says they chose False (declined all options), which in many game engines means passing on casting anything this phase. If they can still cast in later phases, this is fine sequencing. But given that this appears to be the precombat main phase and they might have post-combat opportunities, this could be acceptable. However, casting Burst Lightning pre-combat on the opponent would enable Hired Claw's +1/+1 counter ability (requires opponent lost life this turn), making attacks stronger. This is a missed optimization at minimum.",
